# Gantry

## Overview

Gantry is a crane-building puzzle, played in the browser in a 3D construction
yard. Each site sets out anchor points, a handful of loads, and the pads they
must be delivered to. The player builds a crane out of struts, cables, and rails
on a lattice, mounts a slew ring and a trolley track, then writes an instruction
tape that drives the crane's four axes: slewing the arm, driving the trolley,
hoisting the cable, and turning the grip. Running the tape plays it out under a
structural simulation: every member carries a computed force, an overloaded
member breaks, and a load swings on its cable as the crane moves it.

A site is cleared when every load has been set down on its pad. The score is the
crane's cost and the tape's running time, so a cheap crane driven briskly beats
an overbuilt one driven timidly. Driving briskly has a price: moving faster
loads the structure harder and swings the load wider, so speed is bought with
steel.

Gantry has its own name, look, and rules, and its assets, branding, and design
are original to it.

The specification spans several files under `specs/`. `specs/world.md` gives the
world frame, the lattice, and the anatomy of a site; `specs/structure.md` the
members, materials, and parts a crane is built from and the rules the editor
enforces; `specs/statics.md` how member forces are computed and how the
structure fails; `specs/rigging.md` the hoist cable, the hook, the swinging
load, and attaching and releasing; `specs/program.md` the instruction tape and
the axis motion it commands; `specs/controls.md` the camera, the pointer, and
the key actions; `specs/state.md` what the game's state carries;
`specs/instrumentation.md` the debug and automation surface; `specs/ui.md` the
screens, the readouts, and the audio; `specs/sites.md` the fixed set of sites;
and `specs/assets.md` the assets the build produces and ships. Read all of them
and build the game they describe as one cohesive whole.

