### The checks the repository passes

Four commands run over the finished repository before it is reviewed:

| Command | Checks |
| --- | --- |
| `npx tsc --noEmit` | The code type-checks. A repository that does not compile is not reviewed. |
| `npx eslint .` | The code is lint-clean. |
| `npx prettier --check .` | The code is formatted. |
| `npx vitest run --coverage` | Your tests pass, with their count and coverage reported. |

They run on the repository as you leave it. `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`,
`npm run format`, and `npm test` run the same four locally.

### The build interface

`npm ci` followed by `npm run build` produces the complete static site into
`dist/` at the repository root, with an `index.html` at the root of that
directory as the entry point. That directory runs correctly when served as-is at
the root of any static file server, and equally when served from a sub-path, so
every asset reference in the build is relative rather than root-absolute. The
scripts that do this are already in `package.json`.

The build is self-contained. The asset tools on this machine's `PATH` are
development tools for producing the files under `assets/`; the produced files
are committed, the build bundles them, and neither `npm ci` nor `npm run build`
invokes a tool. `specs/assets.md` states what is produced.

## Goal of this build

Produce a complete, polished, playable game that runs entirely in a browser.
This is a substantial build: a 3D editor with pointer picking on a lattice, a
structural solver that runs on every simulation tick, an instruction tape and
the choreography it drives, a swinging load, six authored sites, several screens
and menus, and a produced set of models and sounds. Aim for a game a person
would enjoy playing, where a collapse is legible and a clean lift is
satisfying.

